# Keeps the docker-compose build context small - source is bind-mounted at
# runtime anyway (see docker-compose.yml), so none of this ever needs to
# reach the Docker daemon at build time. Mirrors .gitignore's build-
# artifact entries.
#
# build/build_release matter for a stronger reason too:
# Dockerfile.linux-release actually COPYs the build context in
# (Dockerfile.linux-ci only bind-mounts, never COPYs) - a stale host
# build/CMakeCache.txt (CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=/usr/bin/c++, host absolute
# paths) getting copied into a fresh Rocky-8-based release build fails
# immediately - confirmed by hitting exactly this failure before adding
# this entry.
.git
**/build
**/build_release
**/generated
**/generated_tcl
**/__pycache__
src/lefdef/**/lib
src/lefdef/**/include
src/lefdef/**/bin
# lef_lib's own BUILD_IN_SOURCE Makefile scatters these directly into
# src/lefdef/lef's subdirectories (.gitignore has the same
# entries) - a stale one left on the host by an earlier native/Docker
# build (e.g. an arm64 Linux .o from a Docker run on this Apple Silicon
# Mac) getting copied into a fresh x86_64 release container fails the
# link with a "wrong format"/relocation error - confirmed by hitting
# exactly this failure before adding these entries.
src/lefdef/**/*.o
src/lefdef/**/*.a
src/lefdef/**/lef.tab.cpp
src/lefdef/**/lef.tab.h
src/lefdef/**/lef.output
